{"1-6":{"people":[{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":4}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"G3551","lemma":"νόμος","tr":"nomos","gloss":"law","lang":"g","inPassage":8,"uses":193},{"base":"G0435","lemma":"ἀνήρ","tr":"anēr","gloss":"man","lang":"g","inPassage":7,"uses":216},{"base":"G2087","lemma":"ἕτερος","tr":"heteros","gloss":"other","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":97},{"base":"G0599","lemma":"ἀποθνήσκω","tr":"apothnēskō","gloss":"to die","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":111},{"base":"G2198","lemma":"ζάω","tr":"zaō","gloss":"to live","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":139},{"base":"G3428","lemma":"μοιχαλίς","tr":"moichalis","gloss":"adulterous","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":7},{"base":"G2592","lemma":"καρποφορέω","tr":"karpophoreō","gloss":"to bear fruit","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":8},{"base":"G1437","lemma":"ἐάν","tr":"ean","gloss":"if","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":336},{"base":"G2673","lemma":"καταργέω","tr":"katargeō","gloss":"to abate","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":27},{"base":"G0575","lemma":"ἀπό","tr":"apo","gloss":"away from","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":644}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":2,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":44,"source":"openbible","text":"And the man said: “This is now bone of my bones and flesh of my flesh; she shall be called ‘woman,’ for out of man she was taken.”","from":2},{"book":"GEN","chapter":2,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":44,"source":"openbible","text":"For this reason a man will leave his father and mother and be united to his wife, and they will become one flesh.","from":2},{"book":"1PE","chapter":2,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":42,"source":"both","text":"He Himself bore our sins in His body on the tree, so that we might die to sin and live to righteousness. “By His stripes you are healed.”","from":4},{"book":"EXO","chapter":20,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":33,"source":"both","text":"You shall not commit adultery.","from":3},{"book":"GAL","chapter":5,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":33,"source":"openbible","text":"But the fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, faithfulness,","from":4},{"book":"GAL","chapter":5,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":33,"source":"openbible","text":"gentleness, and self-control. Against such things there is no law.","from":4},{"book":"ISA","chapter":54,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":30,"source":"both","text":"For your husband is your Maker— the LORD of Hosts is His name— the Holy One of Israel is your Redeemer; He is called the God of all the earth.","from":4},{"book":"1CO","chapter":7,"verse":39,"verseEnd":39,"votes":20,"source":"both","text":"A wife is bound to her husband as long as he lives. But if her husband dies, she is free to marry anyone she wishes, as long as he belongs to the Lord.","from":2}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"7-12":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"G0266","lemma":"ἁμαρτία","tr":"hamartia","gloss":"sin","lang":"g","inPassage":6,"uses":173},{"base":"G3551","lemma":"νόμος","tr":"nomos","gloss":"law","lang":"g","inPassage":6,"uses":193},{"base":"G1785","lemma":"ἐντολή","tr":"entolē","gloss":"commandment","lang":"g","inPassage":5,"uses":67},{"base":"G0874","lemma":"ἀφορμή","tr":"aphormē","gloss":"opportunity","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":7},{"base":"G1223","lemma":"διά","tr":"dia","gloss":"through","lang":"g","inPassage":4,"uses":666},{"base":"G1939","lemma":"ἐπιθυμία","tr":"epithumia","gloss":"desire","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":38},{"base":"G5565","lemma":"χωρίς","tr":"chōris","gloss":"without","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":41},{"base":"G1473","lemma":"ἐγώ","tr":"egō","gloss":"I","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":841},{"base":"G1063","lemma":"γάρ","tr":"gar","gloss":"for","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":1041},{"base":"G3361","lemma":"μή","tr":"mē","gloss":"not","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":1068}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ROM","chapter":3,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":13,"source":"both","text":"Therefore no one will be justified in His sight by works of the law. For the law merely brings awareness of sin.","from":7},{"book":"1TI","chapter":1,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":13,"source":"both","text":"Now we know that the law is good, if one uses it legitimately.","from":12},{"book":"1CO","chapter":15,"verse":56,"verseEnd":56,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"The sting of death is sin, and the power of sin is the law.","from":8},{"book":"EXO","chapter":20,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"You shall not covet your neighborʼs house. You shall not covet your neighborʼs wife, or his manservant or maidservant, or his ox or donkey, or anything that belongs to your neighbor.”","from":7},{"book":"PSA","chapter":119,"verse":137,"verseEnd":137,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"Righteous are You, O LORD, and upright are Your judgments.","from":12},{"book":"PSA","chapter":19,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"The Law of the LORD is perfect, reviving the soul; the testimony of the LORD is trustworthy, making wise the simple.","from":12},{"book":"PSA","chapter":19,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"Who can discern his own errors? Cleanse me from my hidden faults.","from":12},{"book":"ROM","chapter":4,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"because the law brings wrath. And where there is no law, there is no transgression.","from":7}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"13-20":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"G2716","lemma":"κατεργάζομαι","tr":"katergazomai","gloss":"to workout","lang":"g","inPassage":5,"uses":22},{"base":"G0266","lemma":"ἁμαρτία","tr":"hamartia","gloss":"sin","lang":"g","inPassage":6,"uses":173},{"base":"G1473","lemma":"ἐγώ","tr":"egō","gloss":"I","lang":"g","inPassage":8,"uses":841},{"base":"G2309","lemma":"θέλω","tr":"thelō","gloss":"to will","lang":"g","inPassage":6,"uses":208},{"base":"G3611","lemma":"οἰκέω","tr":"oikeō","gloss":"to dwell","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":9},{"base":"G0018","lemma":"ἀγαθός","tr":"agathos","gloss":"good","lang":"g","inPassage":4,"uses":102},{"base":"G1063","lemma":"γάρ","tr":"gar","gloss":"for","lang":"g","inPassage":6,"uses":1041},{"base":"G0235","lemma":"ἀλλά","tr":"alla","gloss":"but","lang":"g","inPassage":5,"uses":638},{"base":"G4160","lemma":"ποιέω","tr":"poieō","gloss":"to do","lang":"g","inPassage":4,"uses":569},{"base":"G4238","lemma":"πράσσω","tr":"prassō","gloss":"to do","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":39}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GAL","chapter":5,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":53,"source":"both","text":"For the flesh craves what is contrary to the Spirit, and the Spirit what is contrary to the flesh. They are opposed to each other, so that you do not do what you want.","from":15},{"book":"NAM","chapter":1,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":18,"source":"both","text":"The LORD is good, a stronghold in the day of distress; He cares for those who trust in Him.","from":15},{"book":"PSA","chapter":51,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":17,"source":"both","text":"Surely I was brought forth in iniquity; I was sinful when my mother conceived me.","from":18},{"book":"JHN","chapter":3,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":17,"source":"both","text":"Flesh is born of flesh, but spirit is born of the Spirit.","from":18},{"book":"ECC","chapter":7,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":16,"source":"both","text":"Surely there is no righteous man on earth who does good and never sins.","from":15},{"book":"GAL","chapter":5,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":16,"source":"both","text":"For the flesh craves what is contrary to the Spirit, and the Spirit what is contrary to the flesh. They are opposed to each other, so that you do not do what you want.","from":18},{"book":"JAS","chapter":3,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":16,"source":"both","text":"We all stumble in many ways. If anyone is never at fault in what he says, he is a perfect man, able to control his whole body.","from":15},{"book":"PHP","chapter":3,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":15,"source":"openbible","text":"Not that I have already obtained all this, or have already been made perfect, but I press on to take hold of that for which Christ Jesus took hold of me.","from":15}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"21-25":{"people":[{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":25}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"G3551","lemma":"νόμος","tr":"nomos","gloss":"law","lang":"g","inPassage":7,"uses":193},{"base":"G1473","lemma":"ἐγώ","tr":"egō","gloss":"I","lang":"g","inPassage":4,"uses":841},{"base":"G3563","lemma":"νοῦς","tr":"nous","gloss":"mind","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":24},{"base":"G3196","lemma":"μέλος","tr":"melos","gloss":"member","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":34},{"base":"G0686","lemma":"ἄρα","tr":"ara","gloss":"therefore","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":49},{"base":"G0266","lemma":"ἁμαρτία","tr":"hamartia","gloss":"sin","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":173},{"base":"G3873","lemma":"παράκειμαι","tr":"parakeimai","gloss":"be present","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G5005","lemma":"ταλαίπωρος","tr":"talaipōros","gloss":"wretched","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G0163","lemma":"αἰχμαλωτίζω","tr":"aichmalōtizō","gloss":"to capture","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"G0444","lemma":"ἄνθρωπος","tr":"anthrōpos","gloss":"a human","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":550}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PSA","chapter":1,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":31,"source":"both","text":"But his delight is in the Law of the LORD, and on His law he meditates day and night.","from":22},{"book":"PSA","chapter":40,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":27,"source":"both","text":"I delight to do Your will, O my God; Your law is within my heart.”","from":22},{"book":"PSA","chapter":119,"verse":35,"verseEnd":35,"votes":24,"source":"both","text":"Direct me in the path of Your commandments, for there I find delight.","from":22},{"book":"PSA","chapter":119,"verse":47,"verseEnd":47,"votes":23,"source":"openbible","text":"I delight in Your commandments because I love them.","from":22},{"book":"PSA","chapter":119,"verse":48,"verseEnd":48,"votes":23,"source":"openbible","text":"I lift up my hands to Your commandments, which I love, and I meditate on Your statutes.","from":22},{"book":"JOB","chapter":23,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":20,"source":"both","text":"I have not departed from the command of His lips; I have treasured the words of His mouth more than my daily bread.","from":22},{"book":"GAL","chapter":5,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":20,"source":"both","text":"For the flesh craves what is contrary to the Spirit, and the Spirit what is contrary to the flesh. They are opposed to each other, so that you do not do what you want.","from":23},{"book":"PSA","chapter":119,"verse":97,"verseEnd":97,"votes":19,"source":"openbible","text":"Oh, how I love Your law! All day long it is my meditation.","from":22}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}